  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;H-0148(01) Rev V1 – Site Location Plan; H-0148(02) Rev V1 – Existing Block Plan; H-0148(03) Rev V1 –Proposed Block Plan; H-0148(04) Rev V1 – Existing and Proposed Plans; H-0148(05) Rev V1 – Existing and Proposed Elevations and Section; Flood Risk Assessment by Floodplan Ltd (dated 02 Dec 2024); Design, Access and Planning Statement by HOMZ; Site Photographs; Fire Safety – Reasonable Exemption Statement&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;All plans received and valid 03.12.24, unless otherwise stated&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The site shall only be used as a Residential Children’s Care Home and not for any other uses falling within Use Class (C2), or for any other purposes, unless an alternative use is agreed in writing by the local planning authority.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The new Residential Care Home hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than 2.no children and 2.no members of staff at any given time (unless any substantive changes are otherwise agreed in writing with the LPA).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until details and location of adequate short and long (with details of a covered, accessible and secure enclosure) cycle storage to meet London Plan Standards has been submitted to, and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the details as so agreed, and the storage provision shall be in place prior to the first occupation of the development, and retained thereafter.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;"
  ],
